. esce fortis)).</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-2d9d5860-9ad4-41ce-ae36-c9f1f432231f" endid="#m-1d1f072c-a84c-4f59-a216-69b11d0055c8"><table><tr><td><rend>((hodium))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>lies ((odium))</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-05640bfd-e462-4442-aff8-6addc5c780c7" endid="#m-74a05b9b-7318-4a55-b36d-3677b67c6a31"><table><tr><td><rend>((oste))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>lies ((hoste))</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-9a378b12-9837-45ef-b578-36d2758a9ebc" endid="#m-147a45a8-8fea-4575-95a7-d1c0a2986abb"><table><tr><td><rend>((stolam ... sunt secuti))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>Der Text der aquitanischen Handschriften ist kaum verständlich, die Korrektur in ((Apt 17-78-2 (stolam candide uirginitatis iam in celesti gloria sunt adepti))) beseitigt die grammatischen Probleme, ist aber erkennbar sekundär. Der mutmaßlich ursprüngliche Text (((CT I))) hat: ((florem … suscepisti)). </rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-c972f23b-8893-4b1c-86d0-c91d43c1b18f" endid="#m-9e3ecdfe-617e-4938-af0f-b8caae4157d9"><table><tr><td><rend>((fratres))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>korrigiert aus ((frate)) (Sofortkorrektur des Schreibers).</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot type="global-comment"><table><tr><td><rend>((27, 28, 53, 34, 35, 29, 30:)) Hexameter (((28, 34)) mit metrischen Fehlern).</rend></td></tr></table></annot></notesStmt><sourceDesc><source xml:id="wit-pa-1871"><bibl><identifier type="siglum">Pa 1871</identifier></bibl></source></sourceDesc></fileDesc><encodingDesc><appInfo><application version="0.9.1"><name>Monodi-Zero</name></application></appInfo></encodingDesc><workList><work><identifier>Pa 1871-8-12</identifier><title>Dicite nunc</title><incip><incipText><p>Dicite nunc</p></incipText></incip><contents><contentItem><locus from="8">f. 8, l. 12</locus></contentItem></contents><biblList><bibl>Innoc intr 27 A 28 D E 53 A 34 C 35 